    "content": "A U.S. visa is an official authorization placed in a passport allowing foreign citizens to enter the country for specific purposes (tourism, study, work). Requirements include a valid passport, application form DS-160, photo, and an interview. Apply through the U.S. Embassy/Consulate with fees varying by type. U.S. Embassy/Consulate Key Visa Information: Purpose & Types: Visas are categorized by the reason for travel (e.g., visitor B1/B2, student F1, work H1B). Application Process: Determine your visa type using the Visa Wizard. Visa Wizard Complete the Online Nonimmigrant Visa Application (DS-160). Online Nonimmigrant Visa Application (DS-160) Pay the nonrefundable application fee. Schedule an interview at a U.S. Embassy or Consulate. U.S. Embassy or Consulate Requirements: A passport valid for travel, a photo, and documentation supporting the purpose of the trip. Fees: Nonimmigrant visa application fees generally range from $185 to $315, depending on the visa category, with possible issuance fees afterward. Visa Waiver Program (ESTA): Citizens from participating countries may travel for tourism/business for up to 90 days without a visa via ESTA. ESTA Duration: Student visas require leaving within 60 days of program completion, while other visas have specific expiration dates. For U.S. visa information, visit the official Travel.State.Gov site. Travel.State.Gov",
